      "id": 1,
      "text": "Wesley Chapel, a Methodist church built in 1872 on land donated by Augustus and Margret Bridges, stands as Woodlawn's earliest landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodlawn_cleveland_county_arkansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Woodlawn emerged as a small farming community during Reconstruction after Cleveland County was formed in 1873.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodlawn_cleveland_county_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town's growth in the 1870s and 1880s was fueled by fertile alluvial soils along the Saline River, ideal for cotton and timber.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodlawn_cleveland_county_arkansas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the 1880s, Woodlawn coalesced around churches, rudimentary schools, and a post office that opened between 1901 and 1902.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodlawn_cleveland_county_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "An adjacent cemetery, with graves dating back to 1869, reflects the early burial practices centered on the town's church.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodlawn_cleveland_county_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Woodlawn enjoys a humid subtropical climate, with July highs around 92°F and January lows near 31°F.",
